# Changelog

## Unreleased

### Added

- Presets for glow, harlequin and helix, each recorded end to end in an empty sandbox. Their steps and waits come from `anina init`; harlequin and helix check their result inside the tape (`Wait "27,211"`, `Exec grep`).
- `anina audit --preset NAME [--part P]`: a preset's parts played in every terminal of the matrix, each one starting from the sandbox as prepare left it. Between terminals only what a play changed is put back, permissions and edits that kept size and mtime included (ADR-0016).
- `anina compare A B`: two runs compared with timing taken out (files, screens as text, PNG pixels, reports). From a report it leaves out the clock, the durations, the latencies and the responsiveness score, so two audits of the same program match. Exits 1 on a difference.
- `--embed` on `run` and `audit`: the images go inside `index.html` / `report.html`, one file to share.
- Every PNG anina writes carries the text of the screen it shows, and `anina check` reads it. `run`, `record`, `audit` and `explore` end with that check on the files they wrote, judged by ctime, so a copy that kept its mtime (`cp -p`, `rsync -a`, `tar x`, `mv`) is checked too. A note kept in the output folder, or what an earlier run left there, is for `anina check` to read.
- A tape warns when a `Type` with several words ends in something that reads as a delay: it is typed as text; `Type@30ms` sets the delay.

### Fixed

- Status lines no longer print the machine's paths: a path shows relative to the working directory, or as `~/...`, also when anina runs from `/` or from above HOME. The audit summary printed the full tape path.
- `anina init` writes waits that hold in the other sizes `anina audit` tries. Text new to the session comes first (a closing popup that uncovers old text does not count); after typing, the wait is the end of what was typed and then what the program did with it (new text away from the echo, `Gone` for rows a filter took away); after a scroll, new text within half the smallest terminal's height of the cursor, counted as rows wrap at 60 columns, and `Idle 3` only when there is none; a wait is picked the way the replay matches it and is never cut at a wrap edge (ADR-0015); a wait is at most 24 characters, ends before column 56 and is never a padded row or a counter. Text keys under 0.25 s apart stay one `Type` even when a completion popup redraws the screen.
- `tool/tasks/fullcheck.sh` packages under a new target path on every run. Cargo unpacks packaged crates by the registry's path and never again at the same version, so a reused path, even emptied, verified the workspace against crates an earlier run had packaged.
- A literal `Wait` matches text the terminal wrapped at its edge: a typed line longer than 60 columns no longer fails its wait in the 60x20 audit terminal.
- A preset's sandbox with a socket, a FIFO or a read-only folder (Go's module cache) no longer breaks `audit --preset`, and a second `anina run` can empty it.
- A wrong `--part` fails before the sandbox is emptied and prepare runs; it used to fail after a clone and a release build. A preset is looked up once per run, so a built-in one is extracted once.
- `anina presets` no longer lists the empty folders in `demo/` as invalid built-in presets, and `anina run` refuses them by name.

### Changed

- The run's part line reads `part 1/1 edit · title` (a middle dot instead of a dash), so the output pastes into docs as is.
- One crate became a workspace of nine under `rust/` (ADR-0013): `anina-screen`, `anina-runner`, `anina-render`, `anina-record` and the `anina` binary, plus `anina-codecs`, `anina-design`, `anina-motion` and `anina-recode`, empty for now. Commands, flags and output are the same.
- Modules renamed on the way:
  - `ansi`, `cast`, `teach` -> `anina_screen::escape`, `frames`, `lesson`
  - `engine::tuitest`, `engine::tmux` -> `anina_runner::engine::inner`, `outer`
  - `tape`, `volatile`, `privacy` -> `anina_runner::script`, `masker`, `redact`
  - `render::font`, `gallery`, `png`, `svg` -> `anina_render::fonts`, `index`, `pixel`, `shape`; `brand` -> `anina_render::brand`
  - `record` -> `anina_record`; `sandbox` (`fsdiff`) -> `anina_record::cordon` (`diffs`); `preset::manifest`, `report` -> `anina_record::preset::specs`, `print`
  - `audit` (`contrast`, `matrix`, `measure`, `report`) -> `audits` (`ratio`, `cases`, `meter`, `print`)
  - `explore` -> `mapper`; `init` (`keys`, `passthrough`, `tapegen`) -> `taping` (`input`, `relay`, `print`); `check` -> `checks`
- `presets/` is `demo/`. The CI workflow is `gatecheck.yml`.
- Releases are tagged `v{{version}}` for the whole workspace.
